{
  "$comment": [
    "Proposed Italian patterns for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.it of each rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (seOwned.it, seOwnedLead.it, reserved.G1.it). Not merged: the owner decides (M3 it translator, 2026-10-06).",
    "Coverage: every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns and no it key yet (25 rules). Skipped: selection-translate and jargon (already have it), io-home and engine-claim ('*' only).",
    "Matching as in the validator: case-insensitive with the u flag, on the rendered text (placeholders filled, markup stripped). Apostrophes are written ['’] so both forms match; no \\b next to accented letters (JS \\b is ASCII-only, so Unicode lookarounds are used instead).",
    "Tested on a fresh copy of HEAD c657445 + src/locales/it.json: 0 hits outside the rules' exempt keys; build / --pseudo 0 errors; node --test 58/58. Every rule catches the counter-examples listed in docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/it-qa.md (appendix A); the generic learning words of doc 03 §1.4 ('impara le lingue', 'per chi impara le lingue') pass seOwned.",
    "keywordMap.seOwned extends the existing it entry ('imparare l['’]inglese') with SurfEnglish's English-news / learn-English phrasing and the chunk words ('segmenti' = the app's 'Estrazione Segmenti'), as de and pt-BR now do. seOwnedLead is applied to every H2 of every locale (validate-dist D-8), so its it patterns only match Italian openings. reservedG1 = how-to phrasing kept out of the home title, H1, description and #cta H2 (doc 03 §1.6 M2)."
  ],
